    <div class="Details-content--hidden mt-2">
      <pre class="color-fg-muted ws-pre-wrap">The Xe2 grouped GEMM supports MXFP4 (E2M1 weights, E8M0 scales at group
32) but not NVFP4 (E2M1 weights, E4M3 scales at group 16), which is the
4-bit format NVIDIA-ecosystem checkpoints such as ModelOpt and
compressed-tensors actually ship. Adding it lets those checkpoints run on
Xe2 without requantizing to MXFP4.

NVFP4 differs from MXFP4 on both axes, so it cannot reuse that path.
E8M0 scales are decoded by shifting the byte into the float exponent
field, which produces garbage for E4M3 bits, and the 16-element group
means one K tile of 32 would span two scale groups.

- Add B_DTYPE::NVFP4, appended so existing enumerator values are
  unchanged, and an E4M3 scale decode branch that converts through
  cutlass::float_e4m3_t. Scale indexing is identical to the MX path
  ([N, K/group_size] per expert), so no layout change is needed.
- Add a tile_k=16 policy ladder mirroring the existing w4a16 tiers, so
  tile_k == group_size and the existing scale-reload gate stays correct
  without touching the mainloop.
- Discriminate NVFP4 from MXFP4 by the scale dtype. This also stops E4M3
  scales from being silently decoded as E8M0.
- static_assert that tile_k does not exceed the block-scale group size,
  so pairing a group size with too large a K tile is a build error
  instead of wrong results.

The per-expert FP32 global scale NVFP4 checkpoints also carry is left to
the caller: it is constant per expert, so it factors out of the dot
product and is cheaper applied to that expert's output rows.

Signed-off-by: Rohit &lt;knowrohit.work@gmail.com&gt;</pre>
